            <div>
              <h5 class="font-medium mb-2">AI Model:</h5>
              <ul class="text-sm space-y-1">
                <li>Grok-2 Large Language Model</li>
                <li>Estimated 175+ billion parameters</li>
                <li>Trained on extensive web data corpus</li>
                <li>Real-time internet access capabilities</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h5 class="font-medium mb-2">Infrastructure:</h5>
              <ul class="text-sm space-y-1">
                <li>Custom content generation pipeline</li>
                <li>Automated fact-checking system</li>
                <li>Dynamic content updating mechanisms</li>
                <li>Distributed computing architecture</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 mt-8">Content Generation Process</h3>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Analysis of Grokipedia's output suggests a multi-stage content generation process:
        </p>

        <div class="bg-purple-50 dark:bg-purple-950/20 p-6 rounded-lg my-6">
          <h4 class="font-semibold mb-3 text-purple-800 dark:text-purple-200">Proposed Generation Pipeline:</h4>
          <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-3">
            <li><strong>Topic Identification:</strong> System identifies knowledge gaps or trending topics</li>
            <li><strong>Information Retrieval:</strong> Grok searches web for relevant information</li>
            <li><strong>Content Synthesis:</strong> AI generates encyclopedic entries</li>
            <li><strong>Quality Filtering:</strong> Automated systems attempt fact verification</li>
            <li><strong>Publication:</strong> Content goes live with minimal human oversight</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 mt-8">Critical Technical Limitations</h2>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 mt-6">1. Hallucination and Factual Inaccuracy</h3>
        <p class="mb-4">
          The most significant technical limitation of Grokipedia's AI system is its propensity for hallucination—generating plausible but factually incorrect information:
        </p>

        <div class="bg-red-50 dark:bg-red-950/20 p-6 rounded-lg my-6">
          <h4 class="font-semibold mb-3 text-red-800 dark:text-red-200">Documented Hallucination Patterns:</h4>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Fabricated Sources:</strong> AI generates citations to non-existent books and papers</li>
            <li><strong>Invented Events:</strong> Creates detailed descriptions of events that never occurred</li>
            <li><strong>False Biographical Details:</strong> Attributes incorrect personal information to real people</li>
            <li><strong>Technical Inaccuracies:</strong> Generates scientifically incorrect explanations</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-yellow-50 dark:bg-yellow-950/20 p-6 rounded-lg my-6">
          <h4 class="font-semibold mb-3 text-yellow-800 dark:text-yellow-200">Real-World Example:</h4>
          <blockquote class="italic">
            "Science fiction author John Scalzi's Grokipedia entry incorrectly stated he was the youngest of three brothers when he's actually an only child, and claimed his first novel was published in 2005 when it was actually 2004. The AI confidently provided detailed explanations for these incorrect 'facts.'"
          </blockquote>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 mt-6">2. Source Verification Challenges</h3>
        <p class="mb-4">
          The system struggles with authenticating and properly citing sources, leading to significant credibility issues:
        </p>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-6">
          <div class="bg-orange-50 dark:bg-orange-950/20 p-4 rounded-lg">
            <h4 class="font-medium mb-2 text-orange-800 dark:text-orange-200">Technical Failures:</h4>
            <ul class="text-sm space-y-1">
              <li>Inability to distinguish reliable vs unreliable sources</li>
              <li>Difficulty verifying source authenticity</li>
              <li>Proper citation format generation errors</li>
              <li>Source content misinterpretation</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-red-50 dark:bg-red-950/20 p-4 rounded-lg">
            <h4 class="font-medium mb-2 text-red-800 dark:text-red-200">Consequences:</h4>
            <ul class="text-sm space-y-1">
              <li>67% fewer citations than Wikipedia</li>
              <li>High rate of incorrect source attribution</li>
              <li>Numerous citations to non-existent sources</li>
              <li>Poor context understanding in source material</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 mt-6">3. Bias Amplification</h3>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Technical analysis reveals that Grokipedia's AI system amplifies biases present in its training data:
        </p>

        <div class="bg-purple-50 dark:bg-purple-950/20 p-6 rounded-lg my-6">
